From: nerves_system_fp3 <devs@spin42.com>
Date: Sat, 17 May 2026 16:30:00 +0200
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: fp3p: rear VCM is DW9800W, not AK7374

The FP3+ ships an s5kgm1sp + Puya P24C64E + Dongwoon DW9800W camera
module (confirmed by the postmarketos wiki and by reading the
Qualcomm chromatix `camera_config.xml` from the device's /vendor
partition). The previous DT used `asahi-kasei,ak7374` inherited from
the older FP3 path.

DW9800W is *not* protocol-compatible with DW9714 — DW9714 uses raw
2-byte writes `[posH, posL]` with no register addressing, while
DW9800W is a register-addressed I²C chip:
  reg 0x02 control byte (PD / ring enable / standby)
  reg 0x03 16-bit big-endian DAC position (10 bits, 0..1023)
  reg 0x06 SAC operating mode
  reg 0x07 SAC timing
Trying to drive DW9800W with the DW9714 driver makes the chip click
(because some writes land in valid registers by accident) but the
lens never travels visibly — exactly the symptom we hit.

Point at the new `dongwoon,dw9800w` driver added in a companion
patch. The binding wants a single `vcc-supply` for the analog rail.

Signed-off-by: nerves_system_fp3 <devs@spin42.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm632-fairphone-fp3p.dts
@@ -657,13 +657,12 @@
 		};
 	};

-	/* AK7374 voice coil motor — rear camera autofocus */
+	/* Dongwoon DW9800W voice coil motor — rear camera autofocus.
+	 * Uses register-addressed I2C protocol (reg 0x03 for position). */
 	actuator: camera-lens@c {
-		compatible = "asahi-kasei,ak7374";
+		compatible = "dongwoon,dw9800w";
 		reg = <0x0c>;
-
-		vdd-supply = <&cam_vaf>;
-		vio-supply = <&cam_vio>;
+		vcc-supply = <&cam_vaf>;
 	};
 };
